  "initial_build_notes": {
    "source": "first assistant implementation notes; unverified; immutable Planner takes precedence",
    "text": "Implementation contract (short):\n\n- Requirement -> owning files:\n  - Window title, main loop, input, health bars, floor, game state, restart/quit: game/main.py\n  - Fighter behavior (movement, gravity, jump, punch, health, flash, knockback): game/fighter.py\n  - Constants (sizes, colors, physics, timings): game/constants.py\n  - Package init: game/__init__.py\n\n- State ownership:\n  - game/main.py owns global game state (state = 'playing'/'ended'), player and rival references, input flags, and lifecycle (init/restart/quit).\n  - Fighter instances own position (x, y), velocities (vx, vy), health, attack timers, cooldowns, flash timers.\n  - main.py calls Fighter methods: update(dt, floor_y), punch(), check_punch_hit(other), draw(surface).\n\n- Interfaces (signatures):\n  - Fighter.__init__(x: float, image_path: str, facing: str='right', is_ai: bool=False)\n  - Fighter.update(dt: float, floor_y: int)\n  - Fighter.draw(surface: pygame.Surface)\n  - Fighter.punch() -> bool (True if punch started)\n  - Fighter.check_punch_hit(other: Fighter) -> bool (True if hit this frame)\n  - Fighter.take_damage(amount: int)\n  - Fighter.apply_knockback(amount: float)\n\n- Coordinate convention:\n  - World uses pixels. Fighter.rect.midbottom is anchored to floor_y. Positive x to right, y increases downward.\n\n- Lifecycle:\n  - init_game() in main.py constructs fighters and resets health and timers.\n  - Play: handle events -> update fighters (when state=='playing') -> check hits -> render -> flip.\n  - Win/lose: when health <= 0, set state='ended', print \"WIN\" or \"GAME OVER\", freeze updates. R restarts (calls init_game), ESC quits.\n\nNow I will write the promised files.",
    "truncated": false
  },
